  },
  "articleBody": "So, you’re ready to build your custom tiny home – exciting! You've likely heard us talk about a 'Site Plan Program' at Zen Tiny Homes, and you might be thinking, \"Is that really necessary?\" Absolutely! Think of a site plan as the blueprint for your land, not just your house. It's a critical component in making sure your tiny home dream becomes a reality without a hitch, especially in a place like San Diego where regulations can be specific.\n\nHere's why it's so crucial. A site plan is much more than just drawing where your tiny home will sit. It involves detailed Land Use Planning, making sure your proposed tiny home placement aligns with local zoning and code requirements. This is where our decade of experience working with city and county agencies really shines. We’ll analyze the Topography of your land – whether it’s flat, hilly, or has other features – to ensure proper foundation setup and drainage. We also meticulously map out Power & Water Supply lines, and even Drainage and Septic systems. This isn’t just about convenience; it’s about compliance and functionality. A comprehensive site plan identifies potential challenges before they become expensive problems, streamlining the permit process and making sure your build is smooth and legal. It’s all about creating a smart, practical plan for your tiny home, from the ground up. Ready to get started? Let’s talk about your site! You can reach us at (760) 492-0742.",
